3,"text":" The song is one of the four unreleased demos by the band included in the original motion picture soundtrack to the same name of the film.","title":"White Noise (Linkin Park song)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Quiet & Still is Magnet's debut album, first released in Norway in October 2000 after the dissolution of his previous band Libido.","title":"Quiet &amp; Still"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" In the US, the album was released under his birth name, Even Johansen, and featured his picture on the album cover (whereas the Norwegian release featured a logo).","title":"Quiet &amp; Still"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The album features early versions of "Where Happiness Lives" and "Nothing Hurts Now," which he would re-record for the follow-up album "On Your Side".","title":"Quiet &amp; Still"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" It also features a cover of "Dancing in the Moonlight," written by Thin Lizzy frontman Phil Lynott.","title":"Quiet &amp; Still"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"A Walk to Remember is a 2002 American coming-of-age romantic drama film directed by Adam Shankman and written by Karen Janszen, based on Nicholas Sparks' 1999 novel of the same name.","title":"A Walk to Remember"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The film stars Shane West, Mandy Moore, Peter Coyote and Daryl Hannah, and was produced by Denise Di Novi and Hunt Lowry for Warner Bros.","title":"A Walk to Remember"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Pictures.","title":"A Walk to Remember"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Vennello Aadapilla (English: "Lady in the moonlight") is written by Yandamoori Veerendranath.","title":"Vennello Adapilla"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" This is a romantic novel written in Telugu which contains drama, knowledge, information, suspense and more.","title":"Vennello Adapilla"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Based on this novel, a serial was also made, for which the author received the Nandi award for the Best Director.","title":"Vennello Adapilla"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Nicholas Spa