{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Ashanti Shequoiya Douglas (born October 13, 1980), known simply as Ashanti, is an American singer, songwriter, record producer, dancer and actress.","title":"Ashanti (singer)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Ashanti is known for her eponymous debut album, which featured the hit song "Foolish", and sold over 505,000 copies throughout the U.S. in its first week of release in April 2002.","title":"Ashanti (singer)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" In 2003, the album won Ashanti her first Grammy Award for Best Contemporary R&B album.","title":"Ashanti (singer)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Her second release achieved Platinum status and other top 10 singles.","title":"Ashanti (singer)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Fred Jerkins III, also known as "Uncle Freddie", is an American songwriter and record producer who is best known for his work with his brother Rodney "Darkchild" Jerkins.","title":"Fred Jerkins III"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Jerkins has co-written several hit songs with Rodney Jerkins and LaShawn Daniels, among them "The Boy Is Mine" by Brandy and Monica, "Say My Name" and "Lose My Breath" by Destiny's Child, "It's Not Right but It's Okay" by Whitney Houston and multiple tracks from Michael Jackson's album "Invincible".","title":"Fred Jerkins III"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" He has also produced a number of songs under the Darkchild imprint for artists such as Brandy, Shola Ama, Men Of Vizion, Keith Washington, & JoJo.","title":"Fred Jerkins III"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Rodney Jerkins (born July 29, 1977), also known by his stage name Darkchild, is an American record producer, songwriter and rapper.","title":"Rodney Jerkins"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" He has collaborated with a broad range of popular artists, including Michael Jackson, Janet Jackson, Beyoncé, Mary J. Blige, Mariah Carey, Whitney Houston, Britney Spears, Rihanna, Lady Gaga, Ashanti, Patti LaBelle, Brandy, Justin Bieber, Luther Vandross, Jennifer Lopez, Toni Braxton, Destiny's Child, Spice Girls, and The Pussycat Dolls.","title":"Rodney Jerkins"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""I'm Good" is an R&B song released in 2004 by American R&B vocal trio, Blaque.","title":"I'm Good (Blaque song)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The song was written by Rodney Jerkins, LeShawn Daniels, Fred Jerkins III, and group member Natina Reed, and produced by Rodney Jerkins.","title":"I'm Good (Blaque song)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" "I'm Good" was released as the second single from Blaque's third studio album "Torch".","title":"I'm Good (Blaque song)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The song is also on the soundtrack for the film "Honey".","title":"I'm Good (Blaque song)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" "I'm Good" performed poorly across the world peaking at number twenty-eight on the Australian ARIA singles chart, number forty-seven on the Swiss singles chart, and number fifty-seven on the Austrian singles chart.","title":"I'm Good (Blaque song)"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":""It's Not Right but It's Okay" is a song by American singer Whitney Houston, from her fourth studio album, "My Love Is Your Love".","title":"It's Not Right but It's Okay"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It was written by LaShawn Daniels, Rodney Jerkins, Fred Jerkins III, Isaac Phillips, Toni Estes, and produced by Darkchild.","title":"It's Not Right but It's Okay"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" The song examines a woman confronting her lover about his infidelity.","title":"It's Not Right but It's Okay"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The Call is the third studio album from Joy Enriquez.","title":"The Call (Joy Enriquez album)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Lifestyle Music Group released the album on January 15, 2016.","title":"The Call (Joy Enriquez album)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" She worked with her husband, Rodney Jerkins, in the production of this album.","title":"The Call (Joy Enriquez album)"}],"peer_messages":["Unverified peer answer: Ashanti
