{"evidence":[{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Multekrem is a traditional Norwegian dessert, made by mixing cloudberries with whipped cream and sugar.","title":"Multekrem"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" The cloudberries can be served as-is or heated.","title":"Multekrem"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" It is common to serve the Multekrem with Krumkake or Kransekake.","title":"Multekrem"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Multekrem is also a traditional Norwegian Christmas dinner dessert.","title":"Multekrem"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Øllebrød is a traditional Danish dish.","title":"Øllebrød"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" It is a kind of porridge made of rugbrød and beer, typically hvidtøl, and it is a thrifty dish.","title":"Øllebrød"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" Traditionally bread scraps are used, so as not to waste any bread that would otherwise get trashed.","title":"Øllebrød"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" The idea originated from monastic living, when monks would dip their bread into hot beer.","title":"Øllebrød"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" Formerly Øllebrød could be accompanying all three meals throughout the day, but is now mostly eaten for breakfast only.","title":"Øllebrød"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"The kransekage (literally "wreath cake") is a traditional Danish (kransekage) and Norwegian (kransekake/tårnkake ("tower cake")) confection, usually eaten on special occasions such as weddings, baptisms, Christmas, or New Year's Eve.","title":"Kransekake"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Gooey butter cake (occasionally called "chess cake") is a type of cake traditionally made in the American Midwest city of St.Louis.","title":"Gooey butter cake"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Gooey butter cake is a flat and dense cake made with wheat cake flour, butter, sugar, and eggs, typically near an inch tall, and dusted with powdered sugar.","title":"Gooey butter cake"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" While sweet and rich, it is somewhat firm, and is able to be cut into pieces similarly to a brownie.","title":"Gooey butter cake"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" Gooey butter cake is generally served as a type of coffee cake and not as a formal dessert cake.","title":"Gooey butter cake"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" There are two distinct variants of the gooey butter: a bakers' gooey butter and a cream cheese and commercial yellow cake mix variant.","title":"Gooey butter cake"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" It is believed to have originated in the 1930s.","title":"Gooey butter cake"},{"sentence_id":0,"text":"Amandine is a Romanian chocolate layered cake filled with chocolate with caramel and fondant cream.","title":"Amandine (dessert)"},{"sentence_id":1,"text":" Almond cream is sometimes used.","title":"Amandine (dessert)"},{"sentence_id":2,"text":" As most Romanian cakes, they can be cut and served in 1-serving miniature cakes or as a big cake.","title":"Amandine (dessert)"},{"sentence_id":3,"text":" They are among the most traditional "sweetshop" cakes in Romania.","title":"Amandine (dessert)"},{"sentence_id":4,"text":" The original recipe has layers made out of a fine caramel syrup, flour, cocoa and egg-based dough with a dash of rum or rum essence.","title":"Amandine (dessert)"},{"sentence_id":5,"text":" The layers are heavy with syrup that also has a dash of caramel and a dash of rum or rum essence.","title":"Amandine (dessert)"},{"sentence_id":6,"text":" The cream between the layers is a combination of chocolate buttercream mixed with fondant.","title":"Amandine (dessert)"},{"sentence_id":7,"text":" The setting of the cake is layer, cream, layer, cream, layer, glaze.","title":"Amandine (dessert)"},{"sentence_id":8,"text":" The glaze is specific to this cake, and it's a combination of fondant with chocolate and rum or rum essence, poured over the cake while still slightly liquid.","title":"Amandine (dessert)"},{"sentence_id":9,"text":" These cakes have also a traditional decoration on top with a little bit of the cream and a diamond-shaped piece of thin chocolate.","title":"Amandine (dessert)"}